<article class="env-proposition" id="0110">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0110">Proposition <span data-tag="0110">3.4.1.11</span> <span class="named">(Transitivity)</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation" id="032H">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="032H" href="/tag/032H">3.43</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:composite-homotopy-pullback} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ Z \ar [r] \ar [d]^{h} &amp;  Y \ar [r] \ar [d]^{g} &amp;  X \ar [d]^{f} \\ U \ar [r] &amp;  T \ar [r] &amp;  S } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> where the right half of (<a data-tag="032H" href="/tag/032H">3.43</a>) is a homotopy pullback square. Then the left half of (<a data-tag="032H" href="/tag/032H">3.43</a>) is a homotopy pullback square if and only if the outer rectangle is a homotopy pullback square. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="00UV" href="/tag/00UV">3.1.8.1</a>, the morphism $f$ factors as a composition $X \xrightarrow {w_ X} X' \xrightarrow {f'} S$, where $f'$ is a Kan fibration and $w_{X}$ is a weak homotopy equivalence. Set $Y' = T \times _{S} X'$, so that $g$ factors as a composition $Y \xrightarrow { w_{Y} } Y' \xrightarrow {g'} T$ where $g'$ is a Kan fibration. Since the right half of (<a data-tag="032H" href="/tag/032H">3.43</a>) is a homotopy pullback square, the morphism $w_{Y}$ is a weak homotopy equivalence. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="010N" href="/tag/010N">3.4.1.2</a>, we see that both conditions are equivalent to the requirement that the induced map $Z \rightarrow U \times _{T} Y' \simeq U \times _{S} X'$ is a weak homotopy equivalence. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
